  "releaseNotes": "Added full support for generating imposters from open generic interfaces and classes (e.g., IFoo,\nOpenGenericClass\\<TKey, TValue>), including multiple type parameters.\n\nImposters can now impersonate open generic members across the full surface:\n\nMethods with T in parameters and/or return types.\n\nProperties of type T and properties returning nested generic types (e.g., IEnumerable).\n\nIndexers that take or return T, including multi-parameter indexers mixing T with non-generic arguments.\n\nEvents with generic handlers (e.g., EventHandler), including subscription, unsubscription, and raising\nevents.\n\nAdded support for methods with their own generic type arguments, both on open generic types and non-generic\ntypes:\n\nMethod-level generics (e.g., void DoSomething(TArg value)).\n\nPre–C# 14 imposter types (new IFooImposter(), new OpenGenericClassImposter()).\n\nSignificantly expanded test coverage for open generics:\nPrompt summary: you asked me to write release notes for the newly added open generic support feature, coveri",
